# Trivy exceptions for the backend image scan (.github/workflows/build-deploy.yml).
# Decision 2026-10-12: every entry is time-boxed (exp:) and needs a re-decision, not a silent renewal.
#
# These four findings are the only HIGH/CRITICAL results that still have a published fix after the
# image-hardening and lockfile work (litellm, msgpack, urllib3, setuptools are cleared). Their fixes
# are major version bumps (transformers 4.57.6 -> >=5.10, sentence-transformers 3.4.1 -> >=5.6) that
# touch embedding, reranking and the LettuceDetect verifier, and the test suite mocks those models,
# so a green suite would not prove retrieval still works. Take the bump with real model validation
# (backend/scripts/validate_onnx_retrieval.py, validate_onnx_reranker.py) before the expiry below.
#
# Why these are not reachable in this application (spot-checked 2026-10-12, not exhaustively audited):
# every advisory needs the process to load an attacker-controlled model repo, config.json, local
# model path or chat template. Runtime loaders use settings-supplied, revision-pinned model ids
# (backend/CLAUDE.md "HF model pins"; llama_guard_handler.py pins _LLAMA_GUARD_REVISION;
# OnnxReranker refuses any model id outside its allowlist), no runtime code passes
# trust_remote_code=True, and the app never calls save_pretrained on a tokenizer or processor.

# sentence-transformers: import_module_class trust gate bypassed when the model path exists locally.
CVE-2026-68770 exp:2026-11-30
# transformers: AutoModelForCausalLM.from_pretrained follows an attacker-set _attn_implementation_internal.
CVE-2026-4372 exp:2026-11-30
# transformers: LightGlue loading path overrides trust_remote_code. LightGlue is not used.
CVE-2026-5241 exp:2026-11-30
# transformers: save_pretrained path traversal through chat_template names. Never called at runtime.
CVE-2026-9856 exp:2026-11-30
